-- allium: 3
-- notifications.allium — everything that tells people that something happened:
-- the in-app inbox, outbound and inbound email, activity feeds, dashboards,
-- syndication feeds and the contribution heatmap.
--
-- Scope: the reactive half of the system. Other modules emit domain triggers
-- (an issue was opened, a pull request was merged, a push arrived); this module
-- decides who is told, through which channel, and what they may later read.
--
-- Includes:
--   - Notification: the per-user inbox thread about an issue, a pull request
--     or a pending repository transfer; statuses unread / read / pinned;
--     fan-out audience; mark read / unread / pin; mark-all-read; bulk marking
--     through the API; automatic read-marking when the subject is viewed;
--     unread count and its push over the live event stream.
--   - MailMessage: every outbound email (issue/PR conversation mail, review
--     requests, assignment, release published, repository transfer offer,
--     collaborator added, team invitation, admin new-user notice, Actions job
--     failure, and the account/security mails whose *triggers* belong to
--     accounts/authentication but which are composed and sent here); how the
--     per-user email preference (accounts/User.email_notifications) applies;
--     the delivery queue; subject rules; mail categories (templates). The
--     per-user preference itself is a field of accounts/User.
--   - MailToken / reply-by-email: signed per-recipient reply and unsubscribe
--     addresses, incoming mailbox processing, automatic-reply suppression.
--   - Activity and FeedEntry: the activity log (one Activity per event, copied
--     into the feeds of the actor, the owning organization and the watchers),
--     its visibility rules (private repositories, keep-activity-private,
--     user visibility), the user dashboard, organization/team dashboard,
--     profile activity tab, repository/org/team/user activity APIs,
--     RSS/Atom feeds (user, organization, repository, issue, release, tag,
--     branch, file), the contribution heatmap, and the cleanup cron.
--   - The notifier fan-out: the canonical list of notification-producing
--     events and which modules react to each (see "Notifier fan-out" below).
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Webhook deliveries (webhooks.allium reacts to the same triggers).
--   - Actions workflow triggering from events (actions.allium).
--   - Search-index updates on events (discovery.allium).
--   - ActivityPub delivery of activities to remote followers and the
--     "following" federated feed (federation.allium reacts to ActivityRecorded).
--   - Repository activity/insights pages ("pulse": merged PRs, opened issues,
--     contributors over a period) — discovery.allium owns repository insights.
--   - Site-wide statistics (models/activities/statistic.go) — administration.
--   - Issue subscription (IssueWatch) and repository Watch records themselves:
--     owned by issues / repositories; this module only reads them. The
--     "subscriptions" and "watching" tabs of the notifications page are
--     listings of those records and are specified there.
--   - star_repo / watch_repo activity kinds: declared in Forgejo but never
--     produced by any code path — legacy, not rebuilt.
--   - SMTP/sendmail transport mechanics (HELO, client certificates, CRLF
--     conversion, envelope-from rewriting, header override) are kept only as
--     config; their wire behaviour is implementation.
--   - Gitea/GitHub/GitLab compatibility mail headers (X-Gitea-*, X-GitHub-*,
--     X-GitLab-*): compatibility-only; a rebuild needs one set of list
--     headers (List-ID, List-Unsubscribe, List-Post, reason, sender).
--   - Queues, retries and batching of the fan-out (implementation detail;
--     the spec states the eventual outcome).
--   - The stopwatch payload and the "logout elsewhere" signal that share the
--     live event stream: issues.allium / authentication.allium own them.
--
-- Emits (other modules react):
--   ActivityRecorded(activity)                         -- federation publishes it to followers
--   MailReplyReceived(author, issue, replied_to, replied_to_code, body, attachment_count)
--                                                      -- issues/pulls create the comment
--                                                      -- (a code-comment reply becomes a
--                                                      -- reply in the same review thread)
--   MailUnsubscribeReceived(user, issue)               -- issues records an explicit unsubscribe
--   NotificationCountPushed(user, unread_count)        -- the web client refreshes its badge
--   SignOutPushed(connection, session)                 -- the web client signs that tab out
--
-- Reacts to (names and parameters as the integration's canonical table gives them):
--   issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)                 -- issues only (PRs: pulls/PullRequestOpened)
--   issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)            -- issues and pull requests
--   issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)          -- issues and pull requests
--   issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
--   issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
--   issues/IssueDeleted(issue, doer)
--   issues/UserViewsIssue(viewer, issue)                -- issues' external stimulus
--   pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)               -- poster is pull_request.issue.poster
--   pulls/PullRequestReadyForReview(pull_request, doer)
--   pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)       -- style is pull_request.merge_style
--   pulls/PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)
--   pulls/PullRequestHeadUpdated(pull_request, pusher, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha, is_force_push)
--   pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)                       -- the PR is review.pull_request
--   pulls/PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request, comment)
--   pulls/ReviewDismissed(review, dismisser, message)
--   pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
--   repositories/RepositoryCreated(repository, doer)
--   repositories/RepositoryForked(source, fork, doer)
--   repositories/RepositoryRenamed(repository, doer, old_name)
--   repositories/RepositoryTransferred(repository, doer, old_owner_name)
--   repositories/RepositoryTransferRequested(repository, doer, transfer)
--   repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
--   repositories/CollaboratorAdded(repository, user, doer)
--   repositories/RepositoryVisibilityChanged(repository, doer)
--   repositories/RepositoryViewed(viewer, repository)
--   repositories/MirrorSyncPushed(repository, ref_name, commits)
--   repositories/MirrorRefCreated(repository, ref_name)
--   repositories/MirrorRefDeleted(repository, ref_name)
--   code/PushReceived(push)
--   code/BranchCreated(branch, by)
--   code/BranchDeleted(branch, by)
--   releases/ReleasePublished(release)                  -- publisher is release.publisher
--   accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions)
--   accounts/PrimaryEmailChanged(user, old_address, new_address)
--   authentication/UserSignedUp(user)
--   authentication/UserSignedOut(user, session)
--   authentication/ActivationEmailRequested(user, code)
--   authentication/EmailConfirmationRequested(user, email, code)
--   authentication/PasswordResetRequested(user, code)
--   authentication/PasswordChanged(user)
--   authentication/TotpEnrolled(user)
--   authentication/TotpDisabled(user)
--   authentication/SecurityKeyRemoved(user, name)
--   organizations/TeamInviteCreated(invite, inviter)
--   actions/WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status)
--   administration/UserCreatedByAdmin(admin, user, send_notification)
--   administration/TestMailRequested(admin, address)
--   administration/MassMailRequested(subject, body, recipients)
--   administration/OldActivityDeletionDue(older_than)

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./code.allium" as code
use "./issues.allium" as issues
use "./pulls.allium" as pulls
use "./releases.allium" as releases
use "./actions.allium" as actions
use "./administration.allium" as administration

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Notifier fan-out
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Forgejo routes every domain event through one "notifier" interface
-- (services/notify/notifier.go) to a set of independent reactors. A rebuild
-- should keep the shape: producers emit one domain trigger per event and never
-- call a channel directly; each channel reacts on its own. The canonical event
-- list and who reacts (I = inbox here, M = mail here, F = activity feed here,
-- W = webhooks, A = actions, X = search index, R = federation, P = other):
--
--   repository created / adopted / migrated ......... F(created only) W A X
--   repository forked ............................... F W A X
--   repository renamed / transferred ................ F W A X
--   repository transfer offered (pending) ........... I M
--   repository deleted .............................. W A X  (+ cleanup here)
--   issue opened .................................... I M F W A X
--   issue / PR closed or reopened ................... I M F W A X
--   issue deleted ................................... W X (+ cleanup here)
--   issue milestone / labels / title / body / ref ... W A X
--     (title change that removes the WIP prefix of a PR = "ready for review": I M)
--   issue assignee added ............................ I M W A
--   review requested ................................ I M W A
--   reaction added / removed ........................ (none in this module)
--   pull request opened ............................. I M F W A X
--   pull request merged / auto-merged ............... I M F W A  (+ P: automerge)
--   pull request synchronized (new head) ............ W A  (+ P: automerge)
--   pull request commits pushed (timeline entry) .... I M
--   pull request target branch changed .............. W A
--   review submitted ................................ I M F W A
--   code comment created ............................ I(mentions) M(mentions)
--   review dismissed ................................ I M F W A
--   comment created ................................. I M F W A X
--   comment edited / deleted ........................ W A X
--   wiki page created / edited / deleted ............ W A
--   user signed up .................................. M(admin notice)
--   release published ............................... M F W A
--   release updated / deleted ....................... W A
--   push (commits / tag / branch delete) ............ F W A X  (+ P: push mirrors)
--   ref created / deleted (non-push) ................ F W A
--   mirror sync (push / create / delete) ............ F W A X
--   package created / deleted ....................... W  (+ P: debian repo index)
--   default branch changed .......................... A X
--   workflow run / job attempt, status, completion .. M(job failure) W A
--
-- Account and security mails (activation, email confirmation, password
-- reset, registration notice, password changed, primary email changed, TOTP
-- enrolled/disabled, security key removed), collaborator-added mail and team
-- invitation mail are sent here in reaction to triggers owned by
-- authentication / accounts / repositories / organizations.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Black-box functions used below
------------------------------------------------------------
--
--   can_read_issue(user, issue)      = access/can_read(user, issue.repository,
--                                      pull_requests if issue.is_pull else issues)
--   can_read_code(user, repo)        = access/can_read(user, repo, code)
--   can_read_releases(user, repo)    = access/can_read(user, repo, releases)
--   can_comment_on_issue(user, issue)= not issue.is_locked, or the user can write
--                                      that unit, or the user is a site admin
--   repository_watchers(repo, category) = users whose repositories/Watch on repo
--                                      covers category (issues | pull_requests |
--                                      releases; everything = any watch)
--   issue_participants(issue)        = poster and every commenter
--   issue_mentions(issue), review_mentions(review), code_comment_mentions(c)
--                                    = users @-mentioned (directly or through a
--                                      team) in that text, who can read the issue
--   issue_notification_audience, issue_mail_audience, mail_mention_recipients,
--   transfer_recipients, feed_reaches, activity_visible_to,
--   contribution_heatmap, feed_excerpt: described where they are used.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The mail infrastructure Forgejo talks to: the outgoing SMTP/sendmail
-- transport and the incoming IMAP mailbox used for reply-by-email.
-- from: services/mailer/mailer.go:392
external entity MailServer {
    direction: outgoing | incoming
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- (none: the contribution heatmap is a list of (15-minute bucket start,
-- contribution count) cells; see the deferred contribution_heatmap.)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/activities/notification.go:30
enum NotificationStatus { unread | read | pinned }

-- What a notification thread is about. `commit` is declared by Forgejo but no
-- code path produces it today.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:39
enum NotificationSource { issue | pull_request | commit | repository }

-- The per-user email preference is accounts/EmailNotificationPreference
-- (enabled | on_mention | disabled | and_your_own) on accounts/User.email_notifications;
-- accounts owns the field and the rule that changes it. "disabled" stops
-- conversation mail only — account and security mail is always sent.

-- The kinds of activity-log entries Forgejo produces.
-- from: models/activities/action.go:36
enum ActivityKind {
    create_repo
    | rename_repo
    | transfer_repo
    | commit_repo
    | push_tag
    | delete_tag
    | delete_branch
    | mirror_sync_push
    | mirror_sync_create
    | mirror_sync_delete
    | create_issue
    | comment_issue
    | close_issue
    | reopen_issue
    | create_pull_request
    | comment_pull
    | merge_pull_request
    | auto_merge_pull_request
    | close_pull_request
    | reopen_pull_request
    | approve_pull_request
    | reject_pull_request
    | pull_review_dismissed
    | publish_release
}

-- Which part of a repository a watcher must be watching for an activity to
-- reach their feed. `everything` means "any watch at all".
-- from: models/activities/action.go:134
enum WatchCategory { everything | issues | pull_requests | releases }

-- Mail categories: each is one template family a rebuild must provide,
-- localised to the recipient's language.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:38
enum MailCategory {
    account_activation
    | email_confirmation
    | password_reset
    | registration_notice
    | password_changed
    | primary_email_changed
    | totp_enrolled
    | totp_disabled
    | security_key_removed
    | collaborator_added
    | repo_transfer_offer
    | team_invite
    | admin_new_user
    | release_published
    | actions_job_failed
    | test_mail
    | mass_mail
    | issue_new
    | issue_comment
    | issue_close
    | issue_reopen
    | issue_assigned
    | pull_new
    | pull_comment
    | pull_close
    | pull_reopen
    | pull_merge
    | pull_ready_for_review
    | pull_push
    | pull_review_approve
    | pull_review_reject
    | pull_review_comment
    | pull_code_comment
    | pull_review_dismissed
    | pull_review_requested
}

-- from: services/mailer/token/token.go:22
enum MailTokenPurpose { reply | unsubscribe }


------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An inbox thread: one per (recipient, issue) for issue/PR sources, one per
-- (recipient, repository) offer for repository-transfer sources. New events on
-- the same issue update the existing thread instead of creating another.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:45
entity Notification {
    recipient: accounts/User
    repository: repositories/Repository
    source: NotificationSource
    issue: issues/Issue?                 -- set for issue / pull_request sources
    comment: issues/Comment?             -- the comment that last made it unread
    status: NotificationStatus
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        unread -> read
        unread -> pinned
        read -> unread
        read -> pinned
        pinned -> read
        pinned -> unread
    }

    is_unread: status = unread
    is_about_issue: source in {issue, pull_request}
}

-- One outbound email to one address. Every recipient gets an individually
-- composed message so that no address leaks to other recipients.
-- from: services/mailer/mailer.go:38
entity MailMessage {
    to_address: String
    recipient: accounts/User?            -- absent for mail to a bare address (team invite, test mail)
    category: MailCategory
    subject: String
    sender_display_name: String          -- the acting user, rendered by from_display_name_format
    language: String                     -- recipient's UI language
    issue: issues/Issue?                 -- conversation mail: the thread it belongs to
    comment: issues/Comment?
    code_comment: pulls/ReviewComment?   -- for code-comment mail
    via_mention: Boolean                 -- sent because the recipient was @-mentioned
    thread_key: String?                  -- groups mails of one issue/release into one mail thread
    status: queued | sent | failed
    queued_at: Timestamp
    sent_at: Timestamp when status = sent
    failure_reason: String when status = failed

    transitions status {
        queued -> sent
        queued -> failed
        terminal: sent, failed
    }

    tokens: MailToken with message = this
}

-- A signed, per-recipient address token embedded in conversation mail. A
-- reply token lets the recipient answer by email; an unsubscribe token lets
-- them stop following the issue by email. Tokens are bound to the recipient
-- and expire.
-- from: services/mailer/token/token.go:61
entity MailToken {
    message: MailMessage
    purpose: MailTokenPurpose
    holder: accounts/User
    issue: issues/Issue
    replied_to: issues/Comment?          -- reply tokens for a comment answer that comment
    replied_to_code: pulls/ReviewComment? -- ... or continue that code-review thread
    expires_at: Timestamp

    is_valid: expires_at > now
}

-- One activity-log entry: something an actor did to a repository.
-- from: models/activities/action.go:203
entity Activity {
    kind: ActivityKind
    actor: accounts/User?                -- absent for mirror syncs, attributed to the repository owner
    repository: repositories/Repository
    issue: issues/Issue?
    comment: issues/Comment?
    code_comment: pulls/ReviewComment?   -- for code-review comments
    ref_name: String?                    -- branch / tag the activity concerns
    content: String                      -- issue title, abbreviated comment, old name, release title,
                                         -- or the (truncated) list of pushed commits
    is_private: Boolean                  -- the repository was private when it happened
    watch_category: WatchCategory
    created_at: Timestamp

    feed_entries: FeedEntry with activity = this
}

-- A copy of an activity in somebody's feed (dashboard). The actor, the
-- organization owning the repository, and qualifying watchers each get one.
-- from: models/activities/action.go:701
entity FeedEntry {
    activity: Activity
    owner_user: accounts/User?
    owner_org: organizations/Organization?
}

-- A browser holding the live event stream open.
-- from: routers/web/events/events.go:22
entity EventStreamConnection {
    user: accounts/User
    opened_at: Timestamp
    last_count_check_at: Timestamp
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [mailer]
    mailer_enabled: Boolean = false                         -- ENABLED; no mail at all when false
    mailer_from: String = ""                                -- FROM (defaults to USER); "Name <addr>"
    mailer_envelope_from: String = ""                       -- ENVELOPE_FROM; "<>" sends an empty envelope sender
    mailer_subject_prefix: String = ""                      -- SUBJECT_PREFIX, prepended with a space
    mailer_send_as_plain_text: Boolean = false              -- SEND_AS_PLAIN_TEXT; else HTML with text alternative
    mailer_protocol: String = ""                            -- PROTOCOL: smtp | smtps | smtp+starttls | smtp+unix | sendmail | dummy; inferred from port when empty
    mailer_smtp_addr: String = ""                           -- SMTP_ADDR
    mailer_smtp_port: String = ""                           -- SMTP_PORT; 25 / 465 / 587 by protocol
    mailer_enable_helo: Boolean = true                      -- ENABLE_HELO
    mailer_helo_hostname: String = ""                       -- HELO_HOSTNAME
    mailer_force_trust_server_cert: Boolean = false         -- FORCE_TRUST_SERVER_CERT
    mailer_use_client_cert: Boolean = false                 -- USE_CLIENT_CERT
    mailer_sendmail_path: String = "sendmail"               -- SENDMAIL_PATH
    mailer_sendmail_timeout: Duration = 5.minutes           -- SENDMAIL_TIMEOUT
    mailer_sendmail_convert_crlf: Boolean = true            -- SENDMAIL_CONVERT_CRLF
    mailer_from_display_name_format: String = "{{ .DisplayName }}"  -- FROM_DISPLAY_NAME_FORMAT (DisplayName, AppName, Domain)
    mail_subject_max_length: Integer = 256                  -- hard-coded: conversation mail subjects are truncated

    -- [service]
    enable_notify_mail: Boolean = false                     -- ENABLE_NOTIFY_MAIL: conversation/release/transfer mail
    enable_user_heatmap: Boolean = true                     -- ENABLE_USER_HEATMAP

    -- [admin] DEFAULT_EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS is accounts/config.default_email_notifications;
    -- SEND_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL_ON_NEW_USER is administration/config.notify_admins_on_new_user.

    -- [email.incoming]
    incoming_email_enabled: Boolean = false                 -- ENABLED
    incoming_reply_to_address: String = ""                  -- REPLY_TO_ADDRESS, must contain %{token} once, in the local part
    incoming_host: String = ""                              -- HOST
    incoming_port: Integer = 143                            -- PORT (993 when USE_TLS)
    incoming_use_tls: Boolean = false                       -- USE_TLS
    incoming_skip_tls_verify: Boolean = false               -- SKIP_TLS_VERIFY
    incoming_mailbox: String = "INBOX"                      -- MAILBOX
    incoming_delete_handled_message: Boolean = true         -- DELETE_HANDLED_MESSAGE
    incoming_maximum_message_size: Integer = 10_485_760     -- MAXIMUM_MESSAGE_SIZE (bytes); larger mail is never fetched
    mail_token_lifetime: Duration = 365.days                -- hard-coded: reply/unsubscribe tokens live one year

    -- [ui.notification]
    notification_min_timeout: Duration = 10.seconds         -- MIN_TIMEOUT: client polling start interval
    notification_timeout_step: Duration = 10.seconds        -- TIMEOUT_STEP
    notification_max_timeout: Duration = 60.seconds         -- MAX_TIMEOUT
    event_source_update_time: Duration = 10.seconds         -- EVENT_SOURCE_UPDATE_TIME; 0 disables the live stream
    notification_page_size: Integer = 20                    -- inbox default page size

    -- [ui] / [other]
    feed_max_commit_num: Integer = 5                        -- FEED_MAX_COMMIT_NUM: commits kept per push activity
    feed_paging_num: Integer = 20                           -- FEED_PAGING_NUM: dashboard page size, release-feed cap
    feed_comment_excerpt_max: Integer = 200                 -- hard-coded: activity comment excerpt length
    enable_feed: Boolean = true                             -- [other] ENABLE_FEED: RSS/Atom endpoints

    -- [cron.delete_old_actions] ENABLED=false, SCHEDULE=@every 168h,
    -- OLDER_THAN=8760h: owned by administration's cron registry.

    -- heatmap shape (hard-coded)
    heatmap_window: Duration = 371.days                     -- 53 full weeks
    heatmap_bucket: Duration = 15.minutes
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inbox: fan-out of issue / pull request events
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Two internal triggers carry every inbox delivery:
--   IssueThreadActivity(issue, comment, author)          -> everyone in the audience
--   IssueThreadActivityFor(issue, comment, author, receiver) -> one named receiver
-- The audience of an issue thread is:
--   (issue subscribers) + (repository watchers of the issue's kind, except
--   while a pull request title carries a work-in-progress prefix) +
--   (participants: poster and commenters)
--   minus the author, minus users who explicitly unsubscribed from the issue,
--   minus users who have blocked the author.
-- A named receiver (a mention, an assignee, a requested reviewer) bypasses the
-- audience filters but not the read-permission check.

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:91
rule InboxOnIssueOpened {
    when: issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)
    requires: not issue.is_pull
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: issue, comment: null, author: issue.poster)
    ensures:
        for m in mentions:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: null, author: issue.poster, receiver: m)
}

-- A new pull request goes to pull-request watchers and participants, minus
-- the poster, plus mentions — all as named receivers.
-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:131
rule InboxOnPullRequestOpened {
    when: pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    let issue = pull_request.issue
    let mentions = issue_mentions(issue)
    let receivers = (repository_watchers(issue.repository, pull_requests) + issue_participants(issue) - {issue.poster}) + mentions
    ensures:
        for r in receivers:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: null, author: issue.poster, receiver: r)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:64
rule InboxOnComment {
    when: issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: doer)
    ensures:
        for m in mentions:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: doer, receiver: m)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:105
rule InboxOnIssueClosed {
    when: issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: doer)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:105
rule InboxOnIssueReopened {
    when: issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: doer)
}

-- Removing the work-in-progress prefix from a pull request title tells the
-- audience it is ready for review.
-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:113
rule InboxOnReadyForReview {
    when: pulls/PullRequestReadyForReview(pull_request, doer)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: doer)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:124
rule InboxOnPullRequestMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    -- an auto-merge is announced once, by the PullRequestAutoMerged rule
    requires: not pull_request.merged_automatically
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: merger)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:128
rule InboxOnPullRequestAutoMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: merger)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:166
rule InboxOnReviewSubmitted {
    when: pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)
    let issue = review.pull_request.issue
    let mentions = review_mentions(review)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: issue, comment: null, author: review.reviewer)
    ensures:
        for m in mentions:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: null, author: review.reviewer, receiver: m)
}

-- A stand-alone code comment notifies only the people it mentions.
-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:188
rule InboxOnCodeComment {
    when: pulls/PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request, comment)
    let mentions = code_comment_mentions(comment)
    ensures:
        for m in mentions:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: comment.poster, receiver: m)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:199
rule InboxOnPullRequestCommitsPushed {
    when: pulls/PullRequestHeadUpdated(pull_request, pusher, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha, is_force_push)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: pusher)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:208
rule InboxOnReviewDismissed {
    when: pulls/ReviewDismissed(review, dismisser, message)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivity(issue: review.pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: dismisser)
}

-- Being assigned by somebody else notifies the assignee. Unassignment and
-- self-assignment notify nobody.
-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:217
rule InboxOnAssigned {
    when: issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
    requires: not removed
    requires: doer != assignee
    ensures: IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: doer, receiver: assignee)
}

-- from: services/uinotification/notify.go:233
rule InboxOnReviewRequested {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
    ensures: IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, author: requester, receiver: reviewer)
}

-- Expand an audience-wide event into one delivery per audience member.
-- from: models/activities/notification_list.go:85
rule ExpandIssueThreadAudience {
    when: IssueThreadActivity(issue, comment, author)
    let audience = issue_notification_audience(issue, author)
    ensures:
        for r in audience:
            IssueThreadActivityFor(issue: issue, comment: comment, author: author, receiver: r)
    @guidance
        -- issue_notification_audience(issue, author) =
        --   issues/subscribers(issue)
        --   + (repository_watchers(repo, issues | pull_requests by kind)
        --      unless the issue is a pull request whose title has a WIP prefix)
        --   + issue_participants(issue)
        --   - {author}
        --   - issues/explicitly_unsubscribed(issue)
        --   - users who have blocked the author (accounts/UserBlock)
}

-- Deliver to one receiver: create the thread, or bring an existing one back.
-- A read thread becomes unread and points at the new comment; an unread or
-- pinned thread keeps its status and only moves to the top.
-- from: models/activities/notification_list.go:155
rule DeliverIssueNotification {
    when: IssueThreadActivityFor(issue, comment, author, receiver)
    requires: can_read_issue(receiver, issue)
    let existing = Notification{recipient: receiver, issue: issue}
    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            if existing.status = read:
                existing.status = unread
                existing.comment = comment
            existing.updated_at = now
        else:
            Notification.created(
                recipient: receiver,
                repository: issue.repository,
                source: if issue.is_pull: pull_request else: issue,
                issue: issue,
                comment: comment,
                status: unread,
                created_at: now,
                updated_at: now
            )
    @guidance
        -- Deleted receivers are skipped silently. Delivery is asynchronous
        -- (a queue) in Forgejo; only the eventual outcome is normative.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inbox: repository transfer offers
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A pending transfer notifies the receiving user, or — for an organization —
-- every member allowed to create repositories in it.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:69
rule InboxOnRepoTransferOffered {
    when: repositories/RepositoryTransferRequested(repository, doer, transfer)
    let receivers = transfer_recipients(transfer)
    ensures:
        for r in receivers:
            Notification.created(
                recipient: r,
                repository: transfer.repository,
                source: repository,
                issue: null,
                comment: null,
                status: unread,
                created_at: now,
                updated_at: now
            )
    @guidance
        -- transfer_recipients(transfer) = {transfer.recipient_user} when the
        -- new owner is a user; otherwise every member of the new owner
        -- organization who may create repositories in it (owners and members
        -- of teams with repository-creation permission).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inbox: reading
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Opening an issue or pull request marks the viewer's unread thread read
-- (pinned threads stay pinned).
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:268
rule ViewingIssueMarksItRead {
    when: issues/UserViewsIssue(viewer, issue)
    let thread = Notification{recipient: viewer, issue: issue}
    requires: exists thread
    requires: thread.status = unread
    ensures: thread.status = read
}

-- Opening a repository's home page marks the viewer's unread transfer-offer
-- threads for it read.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:296
rule ViewingRepositoryMarksTransferOfferRead {
    when: repositories/RepositoryViewed(viewer, repository)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where recipient = viewer and repository = repository and source = repository and status = unread:
            n.status = read
}

-- Explicitly set one thread to read, unread or pinned. Only the recipient
-- may change a thread — not even a site administrator.
-- Web: POST /notifications/status. API: PATCH /notifications/threads/{id}
-- (to-status, default read).
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:306
rule UserMarksNotification {
    when: UserMarksNotification(user, notification, target)
    requires: notification.recipient = user
    requires: notification.status != target
    ensures: notification.status = target
    ensures: notification.updated_at = now
}

-- "Mark all as read" in the web inbox: every unread thread of the user
-- becomes read; pinned threads are untouched.
-- Web: POST /notifications/purge.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:334
rule UserMarksAllNotificationsRead {
    when: UserMarksAllNotificationsRead(user)
    let unread = Notifications where status = unread and recipient = user
    ensures:
        for n in unread:
            n.status = read
            n.updated_at = now
}

-- API bulk marking: every thread of the user whose status is in
-- `from_statuses` (default {unread}; all statuses when the caller asks for
-- "all") and that was last updated at or before `updated_before` is moved to
-- `to_status` (default read).
-- API: PUT /notifications (last_read_at, all, status-types, to-status).
-- from: routers/api/v1/notify/user.go:94
rule UserMarksNotificationsInBulk {
    when: UserMarksNotificationsInBulk(user, from_statuses, to_status, updated_before)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where recipient = user and status in from_statuses and updated_at <= updated_before:
            n.status = to_status
            n.updated_at = now
}

-- The same, restricted to one repository.
-- API: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/notifications.
-- from: routers/api/v1/notify/repo.go:134
rule UserMarksRepoNotificationsInBulk {
    when: UserMarksRepoNotificationsInBulk(user, repository, from_statuses, to_status, updated_before)
    requires: can_read_code(user, repository)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where recipient = user and repository = repository and status in from_statuses and updated_at <= updated_before:
            n.status = to_status
            n.updated_at = now
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inbox: live unread count
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A signed-in browser opens the live event stream. Anonymous visitors are
-- told the stream is closed ("unauthorized") and get nothing else.
-- Web: GET /user/events (server-sent events, ping every 30s).
-- from: routers/web/events/events.go:22
rule UserOpensEventStream {
    when: UserOpensEventStream(user)
    requires: config.event_source_update_time > 0.seconds
    ensures: EventStreamConnection.created(user: user, opened_at: now, last_count_check_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/web/events/events.go:88
rule UserClosesEventStream {
    when: UserClosesEventStream(connection)
    ensures: not exists connection
}

-- Every update interval, each connected user whose threads changed since the
-- last check is pushed their current unread count.
-- from: modules/eventsource/manager_run.go:74
rule PushUnreadCount {
    when: connection: EventStreamConnection.last_count_check_at + config.event_source_update_time <= now
    let changed = Notifications where recipient = connection.user and updated_at >= connection.last_count_check_at
    let unread = Notifications where recipient = connection.user and status = unread
    ensures: connection.last_count_check_at = now
    ensures:
        if changed.count > 0:
            NotificationCountPushed(user: connection.user, unread_count: unread.count)
    @guidance
        -- When no stream is connected, clients fall back to polling
        -- GET /notifications/new (web) or GET /api/v1/notifications/new with
        -- a back-off from notification_min_timeout by notification_timeout_step
        -- up to notification_max_timeout.
}

-- Signing out tells the user's other open tabs, which sign themselves out
-- ("logout" event: "here" for the tab of that session, "elsewhere" otherwise).
-- from: routers/web/events/events.go:88
rule SignOutReachesOpenTabs {
    when: authentication/UserSignedOut(user, session)
    ensures:
        for c in EventStreamConnections where user = user:
            SignOutPushed(connection: c, session: session)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inbox: cleanup
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/issue/issue.go:275
rule DeleteNotificationsOfDeletedIssue {
    when: issues/IssueDeleted(issue, doer)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where issue = issue:
            not exists n
}

-- from: services/repository/delete.go:190
rule DeleteNotificationsOfDeletedRepository {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where repository = repository:
            not exists n
}

-- from: services/user/delete.go:111
rule DeleteInboxAndFeedOfDeletedUser {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions)
    ensures:
        for n in Notifications where recipient = user:
            not exists n
    ensures:
        for e in FeedEntries where owner_user = user:
            not exists e
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email: conversation mail (issues and pull requests)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Two internal triggers carry every conversation mail:
--   IssueMailDue(issue, doer, category, comment, mentions, force_doer)
--   IssueMailFor(issue, doer, category, comment, recipient, via_mention)
-- Audience for IssueMailDue:
--   mentions (who need preference enabled / and_your_own / on_mention), then
--   poster + assignees + participants + subscribers + repository watchers
--   (watchers only when the issue is not a WIP pull request, or the event is
--   the pull request being opened) — who need preference enabled / and_your_own;
--   minus explicit unsubscribers; minus the doer unless the doer chose
--   and_your_own or force_doer is set (auto-merge); each recipient must be an
--   active, login-permitted individual user able to read the issue's unit.

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:48
rule MailOnIssueOpened {
    when: issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)
    requires: not issue.is_pull
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: issue, doer: issue.poster, category: issue_new, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: mentions, force_doer: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:89
rule MailOnPullRequestOpened {
    when: pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    let mentions = issue_mentions(pull_request.issue)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: pull_request.issue.poster, category: pull_new, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: mentions, force_doer: false)
}

-- The mail category follows the comment kind: plain comment, close, reopen,
-- code comment, or pull-request push.
-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:25
rule MailOnComment {
    when: issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
    let category = comment_mail_category(comment)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: category, comment: comment, code_comment: null, mentions: mentions, force_doer: false)
}

-- When an issue is closed by a commit or a merged pull request, the mail says
-- which commit closed it.
-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:52
rule MailOnIssueClosed {
    when: issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)
    let category = if issue.is_pull: pull_close else: issue_close
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: category, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:52
rule MailOnIssueReopened {
    when: issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)
    let category = if issue.is_pull: pull_reopen else: issue_reopen
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: category, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:78
rule MailOnReadyForReview {
    when: pulls/PullRequestReadyForReview(pull_request, doer)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: doer, category: pull_ready_for_review, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:132
rule MailOnPullRequestMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    -- an auto-merge is announced once, by the PullRequestAutoMerged rule
    requires: not pull_request.merged_automatically
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: merger, category: pull_merge, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- An automatic merge also mails the person who scheduled it.
-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:142
rule MailOnPullRequestAutoMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: merger, category: pull_merge, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: true)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:94
rule MailOnReviewSubmitted {
    when: pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)
    let category = review_mail_category(review)
    let mentions = review_mentions(review)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: review.pull_request.issue, doer: review.reviewer, category: category, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: mentions, force_doer: false)
    @guidance
        -- review_mail_category: approve -> pull_review_approve,
        -- request_changes -> pull_review_reject, comment -> pull_review_comment.
        -- The mail body lists the review's code comments.
}

-- A stand-alone code comment mails only its mentions (never the poster).
-- from: services/mailer/mail_comment.go:42
rule MailOnCodeComment {
    when: pulls/PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request, comment)
    let mentions = code_comment_mentions(comment)
    let recipients = mail_mention_recipients(pull_request.issue, comment.poster, mentions, false)
    ensures:
        for r in recipients:
            IssueMailFor(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: comment.poster, category: pull_code_comment, comment: null, code_comment: comment, recipient: r, via_mention: true)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:152
rule MailOnPullRequestCommitsPushed {
    when: pulls/PullRequestHeadUpdated(pull_request, pusher, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha, is_force_push)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: pusher, category: pull_push, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:176
rule MailOnReviewDismissed {
    when: pulls/ReviewDismissed(review, dismisser, message)
    ensures: IssueMailDue(issue: review.pull_request.issue, doer: dismisser, category: pull_review_dismissed, comment: null, code_comment: null, mentions: {}, force_doer: false)
}

-- Assignment mail goes to the assignee only, when assigned by somebody else
-- and the assignee has not disabled email.
-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:115
rule MailOnAssigned {
    when: issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
    requires: not removed
    requires: doer != assignee
    requires: assignee.email_notifications != disabled
    requires: assignee.is_active
    ensures: IssueMailFor(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: issue_assigned, comment: comment, code_comment: null, recipient: assignee, via_mention: false)
}

-- from: services/mailer/notify.go:123
rule MailOnReviewRequested {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
    requires: requester != reviewer
    requires: reviewer.email_notifications != disabled
    requires: reviewer.is_active
    ensures: IssueMailFor(issue: pull_request.issue, doer: requester, category: pull_review_requested, comment: null, code_comment: null, recipient: reviewer, via_mention: false)
}

-- Resolve the audience of a conversation mail.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_issue.go:57
rule ExpandIssueMailAudience {
    when: IssueMailDue(issue, doer, category, comment, code_comment, mentions, force_doer)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: config.enable_notify_mail
    let by_mention = mail_mention_recipients(issue, doer, mentions, force_doer)
    let others = issue_mail_audience(issue, doer, category, force_doer) - by_mention
    ensures:
        for r in by_mention:
            IssueMailFor(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: category, comment: comment, code_comment: code_comment, recipient: r, via_mention: true)
    ensures:
        for r in others:
            IssueMailFor(issue: issue, doer: doer, category: category, comment: comment, code_comment: code_comment, recipient: r, via_mention: false)
}

-- Compose one conversation mail for one recipient. With incoming email
-- enabled it carries a personal reply address (when the subject supports
-- replies: the issue itself, a comment, a review or a code comment — not a
-- push notice) and a personal unsubscribe address.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:223
rule ComposeIssueMail {
    when: IssueMailFor(issue, doer, category, comment, code_comment, recipient, via_mention)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: can_read_issue(recipient, issue)
    ensures:
        let message = MailMessage.created(
            to_address: recipient.primary_email,
            recipient: recipient,
            category: category,
            subject: issue_mail_subject(issue, category, recipient.language),
            sender_display_name: mail_sender_name(doer),
            language: recipient.language,
            issue: issue,
            comment: comment,
            code_comment: code_comment,
            via_mention: via_mention,
            thread_key: issue_thread_key(issue),
            status: queued,
            queued_at: now
        )
        if config.incoming_email_enabled:
            MailToken.created(message: message, purpose: unsubscribe, holder: recipient, issue: issue, replied_to: null, replied_to_code: null, expires_at: now + config.mail_token_lifetime)
            if category != pull_push:
                MailToken.created(message: message, purpose: reply, holder: recipient, issue: issue, replied_to: comment, replied_to_code: code_comment, expires_at: now + config.mail_token_lifetime)
    @guidance
        -- Subject: rendered from the category's subject template; whitespace
        -- collapsed, truncated to mail_subject_max_length characters, never
        -- empty — falls back to "[owner/repo] title (Issue #n)" or
        -- "(PR #n)", prefixed "Re: " for anything but a new issue/PR.
        -- Threading: Message-ID is per comment / per state change; In-Reply-To
        -- and References point at the issue so clients thread them.
        -- Headers: List-ID (repository), List-Archive, List-Unsubscribe (issue
        -- URL and, with incoming mail, the unsubscribe address), List-Post
        -- (reply address), a reason header (issue | pull), sender, recipient.
        -- Body: rendered markdown of the issue/comment (empty for close,
        -- reopen and merge), link to the comment, review code comments, and
        -- whether replying by mail is possible.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email: other event mail
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Published non-prerelease releases are mailed to release
-- watchers who can read releases, except the publisher.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_release.go:30
rule MailOnReleasePublished {
    when: releases/ReleasePublished(release)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: config.enable_notify_mail
    requires: not release.is_prerelease
    let publisher = release.publisher
    let recipients = repository_watchers(release.repository, releases) - {publisher}
    ensures:
        for r in recipients:
            if mail_eligible(r, false) and can_read_releases(r, release.repository):
                MailMessage.created(
                    to_address: r.primary_email,
                    recipient: r,
                    category: release_published,
                    subject: release_mail_subject(release, r.language),
                    sender_display_name: mail_sender_name(publisher),
                    language: r.language,
                    issue: null,
                    comment: null,
                    code_comment: null,
                    via_mention: false,
                    thread_key: release_thread_key(release),
                    status: queued,
                    queued_at: now
                )
}

-- A pending repository transfer is mailed to the receiving user, or to every
-- active member allowed to create repositories in the receiving organization.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_repo.go:21
rule MailOnRepoTransferOffered {
    when: repositories/RepositoryTransferRequested(repository, doer, transfer)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: config.enable_notify_mail
    let recipients = transfer_recipients(transfer)
    ensures:
        for r in recipients:
            if r.is_active:
                MailMessage.created(
                    to_address: r.primary_email,
                    recipient: r,
                    category: repo_transfer_offer,
                    subject: transfer_mail_subject(transfer, r.language),
                    sender_display_name: mail_sender_name(transfer.doer),
                    language: r.language,
                    issue: null,
                    comment: null,
                    code_comment: null,
                    via_mention: false,
                    thread_key: null,
                    status: queued,
                    queued_at: now
                )
}

-- Adding a collaborator through the web UI mails the new collaborator.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:193
rule MailOnCollaboratorAdded {
    when: repositories/CollaboratorAdded(repository, user, doer)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: user.is_active
    ensures: MailMessage.created(
        to_address: user.primary_email,
        recipient: user,
        category: collaborator_added,
        subject: collaborator_mail_subject(repository, doer, user.language),
        sender_display_name: mail_sender_name(doer),
        language: user.language,
        issue: null,
        comment: null,
        code_comment: null,
        via_mention: false,
        thread_key: null,
        status: queued,
        queued_at: now
    )
}

-- A team invitation goes to the invited address, whether or not an account
-- exists for it. Refused when the address belongs to a login-prohibited user.
-- The link points at sign-up, or at sign-in when the address already has an
-- account or self-registration is closed.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_team_invite.go:23
rule MailOnTeamInvite {
    when: organizations/TeamInviteCreated(invite, inviter)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: not address_belongs_to_login_prohibited_user(invite.email)
    ensures: MailMessage.created(
        to_address: invite.email,
        recipient: null,
        category: team_invite,
        subject: team_invite_subject(invite, inviter),
        sender_display_name: mail_sender_name(inviter),
        language: inviter.language,
        issue: null,
        comment: null,
        code_comment: null,
        via_mention: false,
        thread_key: null,
        status: queued,
        queued_at: now
    )
}

-- Optionally tell every site administrator about each new sign-up.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_admin_new_user.go:23
rule MailAdminsOnSignUp {
    when: authentication/UserSignedUp(user)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: administration/config.notify_admins_on_new_user
    let admins = accounts/Users where is_admin = true
    ensures:
        for a in admins:
            MailMessage.created(
                to_address: a.primary_email,
                recipient: a,
                category: admin_new_user,
                subject: admin_new_user_subject(user, a.language),
                sender_display_name: "",
                language: a.language,
                issue: null,
                comment: null,
                code_comment: null,
                via_mention: false,
                thread_key: null,
                status: queued,
                queued_at: now
            )
}

-- A failed Actions job mails the user who triggered the run (or, for runs
-- triggered by the system, the repository owner) when the run asked for
-- email notification and the user has not disabled email.
-- from: services/mailer/mail_actions.go:20
rule MailOnActionsJobFailed {
    when: actions/WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status)
    requires: is_failure(job.status)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: job.run.notify_email
    let target = job_failure_recipient(job)
    requires: target != null
    requires: target.email_notifications != disabled
    ensures: MailMessage.created(
        to_address: target.primary_email,
        recipient: target,
        category: actions_job_failed,
        subject: job_failure_subject(job, target.language),
        sender_display_name: "",
        language: target.language,
        issue: null,
        comment: null,
        code_comment: null,
        via_mention: false,
        thread_key: null,
        status: queued,
        queued_at: now
    )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email: account and security mail (triggered elsewhere, sent here)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:98
rule MailAccountActivation {
    when: authentication/ActivationEmailRequested(user, code)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: account_activation)
}

-- Sent to the address being confirmed, not the primary address. Authentication
-- issues the code the mail links to (accounts/EmailActivationRequested is
-- consumed by authentication only, to issue that code).
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:130
rule MailEmailConfirmation {
    when: authentication/EmailConfirmationRequested(user, email, code)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: email, category: email_confirmation)
}

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:114
rule MailPasswordReset {
    when: authentication/PasswordResetRequested(user, code)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: password_reset)
}

-- An administrator who creates an account may have the new user told about it.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:165
rule MailRegistrationNotice {
    when: administration/UserCreatedByAdmin(admin, user, send_notification)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    requires: send_notification
    requires: user.is_active
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: registration_notice)
}

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:602
rule MailPasswordChanged {
    when: authentication/PasswordChanged(user)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: password_changed)
}

-- Sent to the old primary address, which will stop receiving notifications.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:631
rule MailPrimaryEmailChanged {
    when: accounts/PrimaryEmailChanged(user, old_address, new_address)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: old_address, category: primary_email_changed)
}

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:726
rule MailTotpEnrolled {
    when: authentication/TotpEnrolled(user)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: totp_enrolled)
}

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:659
rule MailTotpDisabled {
    when: authentication/TotpDisabled(user)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: totp_disabled)
}

-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:692
rule MailSecurityKeyRemoved {
    when: authentication/SecurityKeyRemoved(user, name)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: AccountMailQueued(user: user, address: user.primary_email, category: security_key_removed)
}

-- Account mail ignores the email preference: it is always sent.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:73
rule ComposeAccountMail {
    when: AccountMailQueued(user, address, category)
    ensures: MailMessage.created(
        to_address: address,
        recipient: user,
        category: category,
        subject: account_mail_subject(category, user.language),
        sender_display_name: "",
        language: user.language,
        issue: null,
        comment: null,
        code_comment: null,
        via_mention: false,
        thread_key: null,
        status: queued,
        queued_at: now
    )
    @guidance
        -- Activation / confirmation / reset bodies carry the code link and
        -- state its lifetime (authentication's code lifetimes). TOTP and
        -- security-key mails say whether another second factor remains.
}

-- The administrator's "send test mail" button, delivered immediately rather
-- than queued.
-- Web: POST /-/admin/config/test_mail.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:64
rule MailTestMessage {
    when: administration/TestMailRequested(admin, address)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures: MailMessage.created(
        to_address: address,
        recipient: null,
        category: test_mail,
        subject: "Forgejo Test Email!",
        sender_display_name: "",
        language: admin.language,
        issue: null,
        comment: null,
        code_comment: null,
        via_mention: false,
        thread_key: null,
        status: queued,
        queued_at: now
    )
}

-- `forgejo admin sendmail`: the operator mails every active account. With
-- "force" unset the CLI asks for confirmation; that is administration's.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:73
rule MailEveryone {
    when: administration/MassMailRequested(subject, body, recipients)
    requires: config.mailer_enabled
    ensures:
        for r in recipients:
            MailMessage.created(
                to_address: r.primary_email,
                recipient: r,
                category: mass_mail,
                subject: subject,
                sender_display_name: "",
                language: r.language,
                issue: null,
                comment: null,
                code_comment: null,
                via_mention: false,
                thread_key: null,
                status: queued,
                queued_at: now
            )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email: delivery
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The transport accepted the message.
-- from: services/mailer/mailer.go:417
rule MailDelivered {
    when: MailTransportAccepts(server, message)
    requires: message.status = queued
    ensures: message.status = sent
    ensures: message.sent_at = now
    @guidance
        -- The configured subject prefix is prepended to the subject, and the
        -- body is sent as plain text only when mailer_send_as_plain_text is
        -- set (or HTML-to-text conversion fails); otherwise HTML with a text
        -- alternative.
}

-- The transport refused it. Forgejo logs and drops the message; there is no
-- retry.
-- from: services/mailer/mailer.go:421
rule MailDeliveryFailed {
    when: MailTransportRejects(server, message, reason)
    requires: message.status = queued
    ensures: message.status = failed
    ensures: message.failure_reason = reason
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email: incoming (reply by email)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A reply to a conversation mail becomes a comment by the token holder: on the
-- issue, or — for a reply to a code comment — in the same review thread.
-- Mail flagged as automatic (Auto-Submitted other than "no", X-Autoreply: yes,
-- Precedence: auto_reply, any X-Autorespond) is ignored, as is mail without a
-- valid token, mail with neither text nor attachments, and mail from someone
-- who may no longer read the issue or may not comment on a locked one.
-- The quoted original and signature are stripped; attachments are uploaded
-- when attachments are enabled and of an allowed type. The incoming mailbox
-- is only polled when incoming_email_enabled, and tokens are only minted then.
-- from: services/mailer/incoming/incoming_handler.go:36
rule AcceptReplyByMail {
    when: IncomingMailArrives(server, token, body, attachment_count, is_automatic_reply)
    requires: not is_automatic_reply
    requires: token.purpose = reply
    requires: token.is_valid
    let issue = token.issue
    requires: can_read_issue(token.holder, issue)
    requires: can_comment_on_issue(token.holder, issue)
    requires: body != "" or attachment_count > 0
    ensures: MailReplyReceived(author: token.holder, issue: issue, replied_to: token.replied_to, replied_to_code: token.replied_to_code, body: body, attachment_count: attachment_count)
}

-- Mailing the unsubscribe address stops the holder following the issue.
-- from: services/mailer/incoming/incoming_handler.go:178
rule AcceptUnsubscribeByMail {
    when: IncomingMailArrives(server, token, body, attachment_count, is_automatic_reply)
    requires: not is_automatic_reply
    requires: token.purpose = unsubscribe
    requires: token.is_valid
    let issue = token.issue
    requires: can_read_issue(token.holder, issue)
    ensures: MailUnsubscribeReceived(user: token.holder, issue: issue)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Activity feed: recording
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/feed/action.go:193
rule RecordIssueOpened {
    when: issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)
    requires: not issue.is_pull
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: create_issue, actor: issue.poster, repository: issue.repository,
        issue: issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: issue.title,
        is_private: issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: issues, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:246
rule RecordPullRequestOpened {
    when: pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: create_pull_request, actor: pull_request.issue.poster, repository: pull_request.issue.repository,
        issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: pull_request.issue.title,
        is_private: pull_request.issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
    )
}

-- The content is an excerpt: the first line of the comment, cut at a word
-- boundary to feed_comment_excerpt_max characters, or empty when the comment
-- opens with a fenced code block.
-- from: services/feed/action.go:226
rule RecordComment {
    when: issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: if issue.is_pull: comment_pull else: comment_issue,
        actor: doer, repository: issue.repository,
        issue: issue, comment: comment, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: feed_excerpt(comment.content),
        is_private: issue.repository.is_private,
        watch_category: if issue.is_pull: pull_requests else: issues,
        created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:213
rule RecordIssueClosed {
    when: issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: if issue.is_pull: close_pull_request else: close_issue,
        actor: doer, repository: issue.repository,
        issue: issue, comment: comment, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: "",
        is_private: issue.repository.is_private,
        watch_category: if issue.is_pull: pull_requests else: issues,
        created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:213
rule RecordIssueReopened {
    when: issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: if issue.is_pull: reopen_pull_request else: reopen_issue,
        actor: doer, repository: issue.repository,
        issue: issue, comment: comment, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: "",
        is_private: issue.repository.is_private,
        watch_category: if issue.is_pull: pull_requests else: issues,
        created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:378
rule RecordPullRequestMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    -- an auto-merge is announced once, by the PullRequestAutoMerged rule
    requires: not pull_request.merged_automatically
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: merge_pull_request, actor: merger, repository: pull_request.issue.repository,
        issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: pull_request.issue.title,
        is_private: pull_request.issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:388
rule RecordPullRequestAutoMerged {
    when: pulls/PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: auto_merge_pull_request, actor: merger, repository: pull_request.issue.repository,
        issue: pull_request.issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: pull_request.issue.title,
        is_private: pull_request.issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
    )
}

-- A submitted review records one comment_pull activity per code comment,
-- plus one for the review itself (approve / reject / comment) unless it is a
-- plain comment review with an empty body.
-- from: services/feed/action.go:322
rule RecordReviewSubmitted {
    when: pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)
    let issue = review.pull_request.issue
    requires: review.status = submitted
    ensures:
        for cc in review.comments:
            Activity.created(
                kind: comment_pull, actor: review.reviewer, repository: issue.repository,
                issue: issue, comment: null, code_comment: cc, ref_name: null, content: feed_excerpt(cc.body),
                is_private: issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
            )
    ensures:
        if review.kind != comment or review.body != "":
            Activity.created(
                kind: review_activity_kind(review), actor: review.reviewer, repository: issue.repository,
                issue: issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: feed_excerpt(review.body),
                is_private: issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
            )
    @guidance
        -- review_activity_kind: approve -> approve_pull_request,
        -- request_changes -> reject_pull_request, otherwise comment_pull.
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:398
rule RecordReviewDismissed {
    when: pulls/ReviewDismissed(review, dismisser, message)
    let issue = review.pull_request.issue
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: pull_review_dismissed, actor: dismisser, repository: issue.repository,
        issue: issue, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: feed_excerpt(message),
        is_private: issue.repository.is_private, watch_category: pull_requests, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:283
rule RecordRepositoryCreated {
    when: repositories/RepositoryCreated(repository, doer)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: create_repo, actor: doer, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: "",
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:292
rule RecordRepositoryForked {
    when: repositories/RepositoryForked(source, fork, doer)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: create_repo, actor: doer, repository: fork,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: "",
        is_private: fork.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:263
rule RecordRepositoryRenamed {
    when: repositories/RepositoryRenamed(repository, doer, old_name)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: rename_repo, actor: doer, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: old_name,
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:273
rule RecordRepositoryTransferred {
    when: repositories/RepositoryTransferred(repository, doer, old_owner_name)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: transfer_repo, actor: doer, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: null, content: old_owner_name,
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- A push records commit_repo for branches, push_tag for tags, and
-- delete_branch / delete_tag for deletions. At most feed_max_commit_num
-- commits are kept, each message cut to its excerpt; the total count and a
-- compare link are kept too.
-- from: services/feed/action.go:410
rule RecordPush {
    when: code/PushReceived(push)
    ensures:
        for u in push.ref_updates:
            if u.ref_kind in {branch_ref, tag_ref}:
                Activity.created(
                    kind:
                        if u.ref_kind = tag_ref and u.is_deletion: delete_tag
                        else if u.ref_kind = tag_ref: push_tag
                        else if u.is_deletion: delete_branch
                        else: commit_repo,
                    actor: push.pusher, repository: push.repository,
                    issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: u.ref_name,
                    content: feed_commit_summary(u, config.feed_max_commit_num),
                    is_private: push.repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
                )
}

-- A branch created outside a push (web UI / API) records an empty commit_repo.
-- Tag creation is recorded by the push path only.
-- from: services/feed/action.go:441
rule RecordBranchCreated {
    when: code/BranchCreated(branch, by)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: commit_repo, actor: by, repository: branch.repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: branch.name, content: "",
        is_private: branch.repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:456
rule RecordBranchDeleted {
    when: code/BranchDeleted(branch, by)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: delete_branch, actor: by, repository: branch.repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: branch.name, content: "",
        is_private: branch.repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- Mirror syncs are attributed to the repository owner rather than a person.
-- from: services/feed/action.go:471
rule RecordMirrorSyncPush {
    when: repositories/MirrorSyncPushed(repository, ref_name, commits)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: mirror_sync_push, actor: null, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: ref_name, content: feed_commit_list(commits, config.feed_max_commit_num),
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:489
rule RecordMirrorRefCreated {
    when: repositories/MirrorRefCreated(repository, ref_name)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: mirror_sync_create, actor: null, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: ref_name, content: "",
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:499
rule RecordMirrorRefDeleted {
    when: repositories/MirrorRefDeleted(repository, ref_name)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: mirror_sync_delete, actor: null, repository: repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: ref_name, content: "",
        is_private: repository.is_private, watch_category: everything, created_at: now
    )
}

-- from: services/feed/action.go:509
rule RecordReleasePublished {
    when: releases/ReleasePublished(release)
    ensures: Activity.created(
        kind: publish_release, actor: release.publisher, repository: release.repository,
        issue: null, comment: null, code_comment: null, ref_name: release.tag_name, content: release.title,
        is_private: release.repository.is_private, watch_category: releases, created_at: now
    )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Activity feed: fan-out into feeds
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every activity lands in the actor's feed, in the owning organization's feed
-- (unless the organization is itself the actor), and in the feed of each
-- watcher who watches the relevant category, has not blocked the actor, and
-- can read the unit the activity is about.
-- from: models/activities/action.go:701
rule FanOutActivity {
    when: activity: Activity.created
    ensures:
        if activity.actor != null:
            FeedEntry.created(activity: activity, owner_user: activity.actor, owner_org: null)
    ensures:
        if activity.repository.owner_org != null:
            FeedEntry.created(activity: activity, owner_user: null, owner_org: activity.repository.owner_org)
        else:
            if activity.actor = null:
                FeedEntry.created(activity: activity, owner_user: activity.repository.owner_user, owner_org: null)
    ensures:
        for w in activity.repository.watches where w.is_watching and w.user != activity.actor and feed_reaches(w, activity):
            FeedEntry.created(activity: activity, owner_user: w.user, owner_org: null)
    ensures: ActivityRecorded(activity: activity)
    @guidance
        -- The actor's own watch never adds a second entry. Otherwise
        -- feed_reaches(watch, activity): the watch covers
        -- activity.watch_category, the watcher has not blocked the actor,
        -- and can read the unit the activity is about:
        --   commit_repo, push_tag, delete_tag, delete_branch, publish_release -> code
        --   create/comment/close/reopen issue                                -> issues
        --   create/comment/merge/auto-merge/close/reopen pull request        -> pull_requests
        -- (rename/transfer/create repo, mirror syncs, reviews, dismissals:
        --  no extra unit check beyond the watch).
}

-- A repository made private takes its past activity private with it.
-- (Making it public again does not un-hide old activity.)
-- from: modules/repository/create.go:273
rule ActivityFollowsRepositoryIntoPrivacy {
    when: repositories/RepositoryVisibilityChanged(repository, doer)
    requires: repository.is_private
    ensures:
        for a in Activities where repository = repository:
            a.is_private = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Activity feed: cleanup
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/issue/issue.go:307
rule DeleteActivitiesOfDeletedIssue {
    when: issues/IssueDeleted(issue, doer)
    ensures:
        for a in Activities where issue = issue:
            for e in a.feed_entries:
                not exists e
            not exists a
}

-- from: services/repository/delete.go:181
rule DeleteActivitiesOfDeletedRepository {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        for a in Activities where repository = repository:
            for e in a.feed_entries:
                not exists e
            not exists a
}

-- Cron "delete_old_actions" (scheduled by administration, disabled by
-- default, weekly, OLDER_THAN 365 days): activity older than the given age is
-- removed from every feed. An age of zero deletes nothing.
-- from: models/activities/action.go:691
rule DeleteOldActivity {
    when: administration/OldActivityDeletionDue(older_than)
    requires: older_than > 0.seconds
    let expired = Activities where created_at < now - older_than
    ensures:
        for a in expired:
            for e in a.feed_entries:
                not exists e
            not exists a
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- At most one inbox thread per person per issue.
-- from: models/activities/notification.go:126
invariant OneThreadPerRecipientAndIssue {
    for a in Notifications:
        for b in Notifications:
            (a.recipient = b.recipient and a.issue != null and a.issue = b.issue) implies a = b
}

-- Issue/PR threads point at an issue; repository threads do not.
invariant ThreadSubjectMatchesSource {
    for n in Notifications:
        (n.is_about_issue implies n.issue != null)
        and (n.source = repository implies n.issue = null)
}

-- A thread always belongs to the repository of its issue.
invariant ThreadRepositoryMatchesIssue {
    for n in Notifications:
        n.issue != null implies n.issue.repository = n.repository
}

-- A feed entry belongs to exactly one feed.
invariant FeedEntryHasOneOwner {
    for e in FeedEntries:
        (e.owner_user != null) != (e.owner_org != null)
}

-- An activity in a private repository is never in a public listing; see
-- activity_visible_to. Recorded privacy never relaxes.
invariant PrivateRepositoryActivityIsMarkedPrivate {
    for a in Activities:
        a.repository.is_private implies a.is_private
}

-- Tokens are personal: a token is only ever minted for the recipient of the
-- message that carries it.
invariant TokenHolderIsMessageRecipient {
    for t in MailTokens:
        t.message.recipient = t.holder
}

-- Conversation mail subjects respect the length limit.
invariant MailSubjectBounded {
    for m in MailMessages:
        m.issue != null implies length(m.subject) <= config.mail_subject_max_length
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- People are the shared actors access/SignedInUser (inbox, dashboard and
-- preferences are personal) and access/SiteAdmin. The two mail endpoints
-- below are this module's own.

-- The outgoing mail transport (SMTP / sendmail).
actor OutgoingMailTransport {
    identified_by: MailServer where direction = outgoing
}

-- The incoming IMAP mailbox that collects replies.
actor IncomingMailbox {
    identified_by: MailServer where direction = incoming
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One inbox thread, as its recipient sees it.
surface NotificationThread {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser
    context notification: Notification where recipient = user

    exposes:
        notification.status
        notification.source
        notification.repository
        notification.issue
        notification.comment
        notification.updated_at

    provides:
        UserMarksNotification(user, notification, target)

    @guarantee OnlyTheRecipientSeesOrChangesAThread
        -- A thread is visible and changeable only by its recipient (an admin
        -- may read another user's thread through the API, never change it).

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /notifications (unread tab = unread + pinned, read tab =
        -- read + pinned; newest update first; page size
        -- notification_page_size), POST /notifications/status
        -- (status=read|unread|pinned).
        -- API: GET /notifications/threads/{id}, PATCH /notifications/threads/{id}
        -- (to-status). Token scope: notification (read / write).
        -- Threads whose repository, issue or comment no longer exists are
        -- dropped from the listing.
}

-- The inbox as a whole: the badge count and the bulk operations.
surface NotificationInbox {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser
    let unread = Notifications where recipient = user and status = unread
    let pinned = Notifications where recipient = user and status = pinned

    exposes:
        unread.count
        pinned.count
        for n in Notifications where recipient = user:
            n.status
            n.source
            n.updated_at

    provides:
        UserMarksAllNotificationsRead(user)
        UserMarksNotificationsInBulk(user, from_statuses, to_status, updated_before)
        UserMarksRepoNotificationsInBulk(user, repository, from_statuses, to_status, updated_before)
        UserOpensEventStream(user)
            when config.event_source_update_time > 0.seconds

    related:
        NotificationThread(n)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /notifications, POST /notifications/purge (mark all read),
        -- GET /notifications/new (unread count JSON), GET /user/events (SSE:
        -- "notification-count" events).
        -- API: GET /notifications (all, status-types default unread+pinned,
        -- subject-type issue|pull|commit|repository, since, before, page,
        -- limit), PUT /notifications (last_read_at, all, status-types default
        -- unread, to-status default read), GET /notifications/new,
        -- GET|PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/notifications (same filters, one repo).
}

-- The live stream a browser keeps open.
surface NotificationEventStream {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser
    context connection: EventStreamConnection where user = user

    exposes:
        connection.opened_at

    provides:
        UserClosesEventStream(connection)

    timeout:
        PushUnreadCount
}

-- What a person receives in their own mailbox.
surface PersonalMailbox {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser
    context message: MailMessage where recipient = user

    exposes:
        message.subject
        message.category
        message.sender_display_name
        message.issue
        message.comment
        message.via_mention
        for t in message.tokens:
            t.purpose
            t.expires_at

    @guarantee EveryRecipientGetsTheirOwnMessage
        -- No message lists more than one recipient address, and reply /
        -- unsubscribe addresses are personal to the recipient.
}

-- A site administrator's view of mail and threads.
surface AdminNotificationTools {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin
    context notification: Notification

    exposes:
        notification.status
        notification.recipient
        notification.updated_at

    @guidance
        -- API: GET /notifications/threads/{id} lets an admin read any thread;
        -- PATCH is still refused for threads that are not their own.
        -- The test-mail button lives on the admin configuration page
        -- (administration.allium emits TestMailRequested).
}

-- The outgoing transport takes queued mail and reports the outcome.
surface OutgoingMailQueue {
    facing transport: OutgoingMailTransport
    context message: MailMessage where status = queued

    exposes:
        message.to_address
        message.subject
        message.sender_display_name
        message.thread_key
        message.language
        for t in message.tokens:
            t.purpose

    provides:
        MailTransportAccepts(transport, message)
        MailTransportRejects(transport, message, reason)

    @guidance
        -- From: "<sender display name> <mailer_from address>"; the subject
        -- prefix is prepended at send time.
}

-- The incoming mailbox hands over messages that carry a token in To,
-- Delivered-To, or a References entry of the form reply-<token>@<domain>.
surface IncomingMailGateway {
    facing mailbox: IncomingMailbox

    provides:
        IncomingMailArrives(mailbox, token, body, attachment_count, is_automatic_reply)

    @guidance
        -- The gateway runs only when incoming_email_enabled.
        -- Only unseen messages no larger than incoming_maximum_message_size
        -- are fetched; handled messages are deleted when
        -- incoming_delete_handled_message is set. The mailbox is watched with
        -- IMAP IDLE and re-checked on reconnect.
}

-- The signed-in user's dashboard: their feed (including private activity
-- they can still see), filterable by day, with their heatmap.
surface UserDashboard {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        for e in FeedEntries where owner_user = user and activity_visible_to(activity, user, true):
            e.activity.kind
            e.activity.actor
            e.activity.repository
            e.activity.issue
            e.activity.ref_name
            e.activity.content
            e.activity.created_at
        contribution_heatmap(user, user)
            when config.enable_user_heatmap

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET / (signed in), ?date=YYYY-MM-DD filters to one day,
        -- page size feed_paging_num. Entries about repositories the user can
        -- no longer read are hidden.
}

-- An organization's dashboard for one of its members, optionally narrowed to
-- one team's repositories.
surface OrganizationDashboard {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser
    context organization: organizations/Organization

    exposes:
        for e in FeedEntries where owner_org = organization and activity_visible_to(activity, user, true):
            e.activity.kind
            e.activity.actor
            e.activity.repository
            e.activity.content
            e.activity.created_at
        contribution_heatmap(organization, user)
            when config.enable_user_heatmap

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /org/{org}/dashboard and /org/{org}/dashboard/{team}.
        -- API: GET /orgs/{org}/activities/feeds,
        -- GET /teams/{id}/activities/feeds (team repositories only).
}

-- Somebody's public profile activity tab: what *they* did.
surface ProfileActivity {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context subject: accounts/User

    exposes:
        for e in FeedEntries where owner_user = subject and activity.actor = subject and subject.activity_readable_by(viewer) and activity_visible_to(activity, viewer, viewer = subject or viewer.is_admin):
            e.activity.kind
            e.activity.repository
            e.activity.issue
            e.activity.ref_name
            e.activity.content
            e.activity.created_at
        contribution_heatmap(subject, viewer)
            when config.enable_user_heatmap

    @guarantee KeepActivityPrivateHidesEverything
        -- When the subject keeps their activity private, neither their feed
        -- nor their heatmap is shown to anyone but themselves and site
        -- administrators.

    @guarantee PrivateRepositoriesStayPrivate
        -- Activity in repositories the viewer cannot read is never shown;
        -- private-marked activity is shown only to the subject and admins.

    @guidance
        -- Viewer may be anonymous. Web: GET /{user}?tab=activity (?date=).
        -- API: GET /users/{username}/activities/feeds (only-performed-by,
        -- date, page, limit), GET /users/{username}/heatmap.
        -- Anonymous viewers see only activity by public users who do not
        -- keep activity private; signed-in viewers also see limited users;
        -- admins see everything.
}

-- The activity of one repository.
surface RepositoryActivityFeed {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        for a in Activities where repository = repository and can_read_code(viewer, repository):
            a.kind when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)
            a.actor when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)
            a.issue when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)
            a.ref_name when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)
            a.content when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)
            a.created_at when activity_visible_to(a, viewer, true)

    @guidance
        -- API: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/activities/feeds (date, page, limit).
}

-- RSS and Atom syndication. All endpoints answer "not found" when
-- enable_feed is off.
surface SyndicationFeeds {
    facing reader: accounts/User
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        for a in Activities where repository = repository and config.enable_feed and can_read_code(reader, repository):
            a.kind
            a.content
            a.created_at

    @guidance
        -- Formats: RSS 2.0 and Atom.
        -- Endpoints:
        --   /{user}.rss|.atom            user or organization feed (as ProfileActivity /
        --                                OrganizationDashboard visibility; private
        --                                only for self/admin; ?date=)
        --   /{owner}/{repo}.rss|.atom    repository activity
        --   /{owner}/{repo}/issues/{n}.rss|.atom, /pulls/{n}.rss|.atom
        --                                activity of one issue / pull request
        --   /{owner}/{repo}/releases.rss|.atom   releases (limit <= feed_paging_num)
        --   /{owner}/{repo}/tags.rss|.atom       releases and tags
        --   /{owner}/{repo}/rss/branch/{b}, /atom/branch/{b}   commits on a branch
        --   /{owner}/{repo}/rss/branch/{b}/{path}               commits touching a file
        -- Branch/file feeds require code read access and a non-empty repository.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

-- issue_notification_audience: see ExpandIssueThreadAudience @guidance.
-- issue_mail_audience: see the comment above MailOnIssueOpened.
-- activity_visible_to(activity, viewer, include_private): see ProfileActivity
--   @guidance; private-marked activity only when include_private; actor must be
--   public (anonymous) / public-or-limited (signed in) and not keep activity
--   private, unless the actor is the viewer, the feed's organization, or an
--   organization the feed's user belongs to; repository readable by viewer;
--   admins see everything.
-- contribution_heatmap(subject, viewer): list of (15-minute bucket start,
--   count) for activities performed by the subject (for an organization: in
--   its feed) in the last heatmap_window, visible to the viewer; empty when the
--   subject keeps activity private and the viewer is neither the subject nor
--   an admin.
-- feed_excerpt(text): first line, cut at a word boundary to
--   feed_comment_excerpt_max, empty for a leading code fence.
deferred MailTemplates.render    -- see: services/mailer/mail.go (templates/mail/**, per-category localised subject and body)
deferred ActivityFeed.visibility -- see: models/activities/action.go (activityQueryCondition)
deferred Heatmap.aggregate       -- see: models/activities/user_heatmap.go

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Inbox and mail audiences differ in Forgejo: mail adds the poster and assignees and uses the *issues* watch selection even for pull requests, while the inbox uses the kind-specific selection and omits assignees. Should a rebuild unify both into one audience definition?"
open question "Forgejo emits the notification for a new pull request with every receiver named explicitly, which skips the unsubscribe and blocked-author filters; is that intended?"
open question "Reply/unsubscribe tokens are stateless and become invalid when the holder's secret is rotated (e.g. on password change). Should a rebuild revoke outstanding tokens on password change explicitly?"
open question "Forgejo sends the Actions job-failure mail from three hooks (attempt, status change, completion) and can mail the same failure more than once; should exactly one mail per failed job attempt be guaranteed?"
open question "Collaborator-added mail is sent only when a collaborator is added through the web UI, not through the API. Should the API path mail too?"
open question "Feed entries are copied per watcher at the time of the event and never re-evaluated when watching stops or permissions change (visibility is re-checked on read). Should a rebuild compute feeds on read instead?"
open question "The `commit` notification source is declared but never produced. Keep it for future commit-comment notifications or drop it?"
open question "The release mail is sent only for non-prerelease releases while the activity feed records prereleases too. Intended?"
open question "Failed mail is dropped without retry. Should a rebuild retry transient transport failures?"

